8. Important production engineering considerations
As an AI Platform Engineer, you should understand when to use each execution model.
Requirement	Recommended approach
Normal short API request	Async endpoint
Chat response appearing progressively	Streaming
Long-running document processing	Background job queue
Large-scale distributed AI workloads	Dedicated workers and message broker
Persistent task status	PostgreSQL or another durable store
Additional concepts to learn:
•	Concurrency: Multiple operations make progress during overlapping time periods.
•	Parallelism: Multiple operations execute simultaneously, often using multiple CPU cores.
•	Backpressure: Prevents incoming work from overwhelming downstream systems.
•	Timeout: Limits how long an operation is allowed to run.
•	Retry: Reattempts an operation after certain failures.
•	Idempotency: Prevents duplicate effects when a request is retried.
A particularly important interview point: asynchronous I/O improves concurrency, but it does not automatically solve database bottlenecks, provider rate limits or CPU-intensive processing.
